WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
In the Netherlands, 26 percent of
the country is below sea level.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.650
Yet millions of people live there.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:12.110
Farms and cities spread across land
that lies lower than the sea beside it.

4
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.330
So why do millions choose to
live below the level of the sea?

5
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.810
Does the land simply decide for them?

6
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.390
In this mission, you'll
sort natural resources,

7
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.610
and test what makes a
land use sustainable.

8
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.210
Then you'll weigh two big
ideas about nature and society,

9
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.030
and check the evidence behind each.

10
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.650
Your mission: explain why millions of
people choose to live where the land lies

11
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:36.990
lower than the sea.
